              "kind": "definition",
              "section": "2.1",
              "subsection": "2.1.1",
              "rawText": "Deﬁnition 1 A set is an unordered collection of distinct objects, called elements or members of the set. A\nset is said to contain its elements. We write a ∈A to denote that a is an element of the set A.",
              "text": "Definition 1 A set is an unordered collection of distinct objects, called elements or members of the set. A set is said to contain its elements. We write a ∈A to denote that a is an element of the set A.",
