              "text": "Definition 8 Let A and B be sets. The Cartesian product of A and B, denoted by A× B, is the set of all ordered pairs (a, b), where a ∈A and b ∈B. Hence, A× B ={ (a, b) ∣a ∈A∧b ∈B}.",
