              "rawText": "We can extend the notation we have introduced for unions and intersections to other families of\nsets. In particular, to denote the union of the inﬁnite family of setsA1,A 2,… ,A n,…, we use the\nnotation\nA1 ∪A2 ∪⋯ ∪An ∪⋯ =\n∞⋃\ni=1\nAi.\nSimilarly, the intersection of these sets is denoted by\nA1 ∩A2 ∩⋯ ∩An ∩⋯ =\n∞⋂\ni=1\nAi.\nMore generally, when I is a set, the notations ⋂\ni∈IAi and ⋃\ni∈IAi are used to denote\nthe intersection and union of the sets Ai for i ∈I, respectively. Note that we have ⋂\ni∈IAi =\n{x ∣∀i ∈I (x ∈Ai)} and ⋃\ni∈IAi ={ x ∣∃i ∈I (x ∈Ai)}.",
