              "number": 1,
              "label": "EXAMPLE 1",
              "title": "What are the domain, codomain, and range of the function that assigns grades to students de-",
              "hasSolution": true,
              "promptRaw": "What are the domain, codomain, and range of the function that assigns grades to students de-\nscribed in the ﬁrst paragraph of the introduction of this section?\nSolution: Let G be the function that assigns a grade to a student in our discrete mathematics class.",
              "prompt": "What are the domain, codomain, and range of the function that assigns grades to students described in the first paragraph of the introduction of this section? Solution: Let G be the function that assigns a grade to a student in our discrete mathematics class.",
              "solutionRaw": "Let G be the function that assigns a grade to a student in our discrete mathematics class.\nNote that G(Adams) = A, for instance. The domain of G is the set{Adams, Chou, Goodfriend,\nRodriguez, Stevens}, and the codomain is the set {A, B, C, D, F}. The range of G is the set\n{A, B, C, F}, because each grade except D is assigned to some student.\n◂",
              "solution": "Let G be the function that assigns a grade to a student in our discrete mathematics class. Note that G(Adams) = A, for instance. The domain of G is the set{Adams, Chou, Goodfriend, Rodriguez, Stevens}, and the codomain is the set {A, B, C, D, F}. The range of G is the set {A, B, C, F}, because each grade except D is assigned to some student. ◂",
              "solutionLine": 1493,
