              "rawText": "EXAMPLE 18 Let A be a set. The identity function on A is the function 𝜄A : A → A, where\n𝜄A(x) = x\nfor all x ∈A. In other words, the identity function 𝜄A is the function that assigns each element\nto itself. The function 𝜄A is one-to-one and onto, so it is a bijection. (Note that 𝜄is the Greek\nletter iota.) ◂",
