              "prompt": "Let A be a set. The identity function on A is the function 𝜄A : A → A, where 𝜄A(x) = x for all x ∈A. In other words, the identity function 𝜄A is the function that assigns each element to itself. The function 𝜄A is one-to-one and onto, so it is a bijection. (Note that 𝜄is the Greek letter iota.) ◂",
