              "rawText": "Remark: Be sure not to confuse the function f−1 with the function 1∕f , which is the function\nthat assigns to each x in the domain the value 1∕f(x). Notice that the latter makes sense only\nwhen f (x) is a nonzero real number.",
              "text": "Remark: Be sure not to confuse the function f−1 with the function 1∕f , which is the function that assigns to each x in the domain the value 1∕f(x). Notice that the latter makes sense only when f (x) is a nonzero real number.",
