              "text": "EXAMPLE 23 Let g be the function from the set {a, b, c}to itself such that g(a) = b, g(b) = c, and g(c) = a. Let f be the function from the set {a, b, c}to the set {1, 2, 3} such that f (a) = 3, f (b) = 2, and f (c) = 1. What is the composition of f and g, and what is the composition of g and f ? Solution: The composition f ◦g is defined by ( f ◦g)(a)= f (g(a)) = f (b) = 2, ( f ◦g)( b) = f (g(b)) = f (c) = 1, and ( f ◦g)(c)= f (g(c)) = f (a) = 3. Note that g◦f is not defined, because the range of f is not a subset of the domain of g. ◂",
