              "id": "rosen-ch2-table-2-3-01",
              "kind": "table",
              "section": "2.3",
              "subsection": "2.3.5",
              "rawText": "TABLE 1 Useful Properties of the\nFloor and Ceiling Functions.\n(n is an integer, x is a real number)\n(1a) ⌊x⌋ = n if and only if n ≤ x < n + 1\n(1b) ⌈x⌉ = n if and only if n − 1 < x ≤ n\n(1c) ⌊x⌋ = n if and only if x − 1 < n ≤ x\n(1d) ⌈x⌉ = n if and only if x ≤ n < x + 1\n(2) x − 1 < ⌊x⌋ ≤ x ≤ ⌈x⌉ < x + 1\n(3a) ⌊− x⌋ =− ⌈x⌉\n(3b) ⌈− x⌉ =− ⌊x⌋\n(4a) ⌊x + n⌋ = ⌊x⌋ + n\n(4b) ⌈x + n⌉ = ⌈x⌉ + n",
              "text": "TABLE 1 Useful Properties of the Floor and Ceiling Functions. (n is an integer, x is a real number) (1a) ⌊x⌋ = n if and only if n ≤ x < n + 1 (1b) ⌈x⌉ = n if and only if n − 1 < x ≤ n (1c) ⌊x⌋ = n if and only if x − 1 < n ≤ x (1d) ⌈x⌉ = n if and only if x ≤ n < x + 1 (2) x − 1 < ⌊x⌋ ≤ x ≤ ⌈x⌉ < x + 1 (3a) ⌊− x⌋ =− ⌈x⌉ (3b) ⌈− x⌉ =− ⌊x⌋ (4a) ⌊x + n⌋ = ⌊x⌋ + n (4b) ⌈x + n⌉ = ⌈x⌉ + n",
