              "kind": "text",
              "section": "2.4",
              "subsection": "2.4.3",
              "rawText": "Many methods have been developed for solving recurrence relations. Here, we will intro-\nduce a straightforward method known as iteration via several examples. In Chapter 8 we will\nstudy recurrence relations in depth. In that chapter we will show how recurrence relations can\nbe used to solve counting problems and we will introduce several powerful methods that can be\nused to solve many diﬀerent recurrence relations.",
              "text": "Many methods have been developed for solving recurrence relations. Here, we will introduce a straightforward method known as iteration via several examples. In Chapter 8 we will study recurrence relations in depth. In that chapter we will show how recurrence relations can be used to solve counting problems and we will introduce several powerful methods that can be used to solve many different recurrence relations.",
