              "promptRaw": "Suppose we have the sum\n5∑\nj=1\nj2\n174 2 / Basic Structures: Sets, Functions, Sequences, Sums, and Matrices\nbut want the index of summation to run between 0 and 4 rather than from 1 to 5. To do this, we\nlet k = j−1. Then the new summation index runs from 0 (because k = 1−0 = 0 when j = 1)\nto 4 (because k = 5−1 = 4 when j = 5), and the term j2 becomes (k+ 1)2. Hence,\nExtra \nExamples\n5∑\nj=1\nj2 =\n4∑\nk= 0\n(k+ 1)2.\nIt is easily checked that both sums are 1+ 4+ 9+ 16+ 25 = 55. ◂",
              "prompt": "Suppose we have the sum 5∑ j=1 j2 but want the index of summation to run between 0 and 4 rather than from 1 to 5. To do this, we let k = j−1. Then the new summation index runs from 0 (because k = 1−0 = 0 when j = 1) to 4 (because k = 5−1 = 4 when j = 5), and the term j2 becomes (k+ 1)2. Hence, Extra Examples 5∑ j=1 j2 = 4∑ k= 0 (k+ 1)2. It is easily checked that both sums are 1+ 4+ 9+ 16+ 25 = 55. ◂",
