              "rawText": "EXAMPLE 21 Double summations arise in many contexts (as in the analysis of nested loops in computer pro-\ngrams). An example of a double summation is\n4∑\ni=1\n3∑\nj=1\nij.\nTo evaluate the double sum, ﬁrst expand the inner summation and then continue by computing\nthe outer summation:\n4∑\ni=1\n3∑\nj=1\nij =\n4∑\ni=1\n(i+ 2i+ 3i)\n=\n4∑\ni=1\n6i\n= 6+ 12+ 18+ 24 = 60. ◂",
              "text": "EXAMPLE 21 Double summations arise in many contexts (as in the analysis of nested loops in computer programs). An example of a double summation is 4∑ i=1 3∑ j=1 ij. To evaluate the double sum, first expand the inner summation and then continue by computing the outer summation: 4∑ i=1 3∑ j=1 ij = 4∑ i=1 (i+ 2i+ 3i) = 4∑ i=1 6i = 6+ 12+ 18+ 24 = 60. ◂",
