              "kind": "text",
              "section": "2.5",
              "subsection": "2.5.1",
              "rawText": "For inﬁnite sets the deﬁnition of cardinality provides a relative measure of the sizes of two sets,\nrather than a measure of the size of one particular set. We can also deﬁne what it means for one\nset to have a smaller cardinality than another set.",
              "text": "For infinite sets the definition of cardinality provides a relative measure of the sizes of two sets, rather than a measure of the size of one particular set. We can also define what it means for one set to have a smaller cardinality than another set.",
