              "text": "Remark: In Definitions 1 and 2 we introduced the notations |A|= |B|and |A|< |B|to denote that A and B have the same cardinality and that the cardinality of A is less than the cardinality of B. However, these definitions do not give any separate meaning to |A|and |B|when A and B are arbitrary infinite sets.",
