              "kind": "definition",
              "section": "2.6",
              "subsection": "2.6.4",
              "rawText": "Deﬁnition 10 Let A be a square zero–one matrix and let r be a positive integer. The rth Boolean power of\nA is the Boolean product of r factors of A. The rth Boolean product of A is denoted by A[r].",
              "text": "Definition 10 Let A be a square zero–one matrix and let r be a positive integer. The rth Boolean power of A is the Boolean product of r factors of A. The rth Boolean product of A is denoted by A[r].",
