        "subsection": "2.1.6",
        "rawText": "EXAMPLE 19 What is the Cartesian product A× B× C, where A ={ 0, 1}, B ={ 1, 2}, and C ={ 0, 1, 2}?\nSolution: The Cartesian product A× B× C consists of all ordered triples (a, b, c), wherea ∈A,\nb ∈B, and c ∈C. Hence,\nA× B× C ={ (0, 1, 0), (0, 1, 1), (0, 1, 2), (0, 2, 0), (0, 2, 1), (0, 2, 2),\n(1, 1, 0), (1, 1, 1), (1, 1, 2), (1, 2, 0), (1, 2, 1), (1, 2, 2)}. ◂",
