        "subsection": "2.3.1",
        "rawText": "Deﬁnition 1 Let A and B be nonempty sets. A function f from A to B is an assignment of exactly one\nelement of B to each element ofA. We writef (a) = b if b is the unique element ofB assigned\nby the function f to the element a of A.I ff is a function from A to B, we write f : A → B.",
        "text": "Definition 1 Let A and B be nonempty sets. A function f from A to B is an assignment of exactly one element of B to each element ofA. We writef (a) = b if b is the unique element ofB assigned by the function f to the element a of A.I ff is a function from A to B, we write f : A → B.",
