        "subsection": "2.3.1",
        "rawText": "Deﬁnition 4 Let f be a function from A to B and let S be a subset of A. The image of S under the function\nf is the subset of B that consists of the images of the elements of S. We denote the image of\nS by f (S), so\nf (S) ={ t ∣∃s∈S (t = f (s))}.",
        "text": "Definition 4 Let f be a function from A to B and let S be a subset of A. The image of S under the function f is the subset of B that consists of the images of the elements of S. We denote the image of S by f (S), so f (S) ={ t ∣∃s∈S (t = f (s))}.",
