        "subsection": "2.3.2",
        "rawText": "Deﬁnition 5 A function f is said to be one-to-one, or an injection, if and only if f (a) = f (b) implies that\na = b for all a and b in the domain of f. A function is said to be injective if it is one-to-one.",
