        "section": "2.3",
        "subsection": "2.3.2",
        "rawText": "Deﬁnition 7 A function f from A to B is called onto, or a surjection, if and only if for every element\nb ∈B there is an element a ∈A with f (a) = b. A function f is called surjective if it is onto.",
        "text": "Definition 7 A function f from A to B is called onto, or a surjection, if and only if for every element b ∈B there is an element a ∈A with f (a) = b. A function f is called surjective if it is onto.",
