        "text": "Definition 9 Let f be a one-to-one correspondence from the setA to the set B. The inverse function of f is the function that assigns to an element b belonging to B the unique element a in A such that f (a) = b. The inverse function of f is denoted by f−1. Hence, f−1(b) = a when f (a) = b.",
