        "subsection": "2.3.3",
        "rawText": "Deﬁnition 10 Let g be a function from the set A to the set B and let f be a function from the set B to the\nset C. The composition of the functions f and g, denoted for all a ∈A by f ◦g, is the function\nfrom A to C deﬁned by\n( f ◦g)(a)= f (g(a)).",
