        "section": "2.3",
        "subsection": "2.3.5",
        "rawText": "Deﬁnition 12 The ﬂoor function assigns to the real number x the largest integer that is less than or equal to\nx. The value of the ﬂoor function at x is denoted by ⌊x⌋. Theceiling function assigns to the\nreal number x the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to x. The value of the ceiling\nfunction at x is denoted by⌈x⌉.",
        "text": "Definition 12 The floor function assigns to the real number x the largest integer that is less than or equal to x. The value of the floor function at x is denoted by ⌊x⌋. Theceiling function assigns to the real number x the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to x. The value of the ceiling function at x is denoted by⌈x⌉.",
