          "rawText": "Suppose that f is a function from A to B. We deﬁne the func-\ntion Sf from (A)t o (B)b yt h er u l eSf (X) = f (X) for each\nsubset X of A. Similarly, we deﬁne the functionSf−1 from (B)\nto (A)b yt h er u l eSf−1(Y) = f−1(Y) for each subset Y of B.\nHere, we are using Deﬁnition 4, and the deﬁnition of the in-\nverse image of a set found in the preamble to Exercise 44, both\nin Section 2.3.",
